# Brahma Fi Smart Contract Security Audit Case Study

## Overview
QuillAudits conducted a comprehensive security audit and dApp pentest for Brahma Fi, a DeFi infrastructure platform focused on automation, portfolio management, and secure on-chain operations.

The engagement focused on identifying vulnerabilities across authentication systems, API security, access controls, ENS integrations, and overall platform stability.

## Scope
- DApp Security Assessment
- Authentication & Authorization Testing
- API Security Testing
- Access Control Review
- Infrastructure Security
- Smart Contract Interaction Testing

## Technologies Involved
- Solidity
- Ethereum
- ENS
- DeFi Infrastructure
- Smart Contracts
- Web3 Authentication

## Key Findings
- Broken access control vulnerabilities
- ENS integration issues
- Missing deletion confirmation protections
- Username validation bypass risks

## Security Improvements
- Implemented stronger authentication and authorization
- Secured API endpoints and user access controls
- Improved ENS functionality and validation
- Enhanced backend validation and platform stability

## Audit Outcome
All identified findings were reviewed and fixed in collaboration with the Brahma Fi team, significantly improving platform security, reliability, and user protection.

